  "summary": "Golf clubs, bags, and accessories. Trend data (May 2026): 'used' searches are dominated by golf clubs — women's golf clubs is the #1 'used' query (search interest 100), with Callaway and Ping leading by brand name. Left-handed and women's-specific clubs trend higher because the supply is structurally smaller than the demand. Boutique direct-to-consumer brands (Stix, Takomo) have small but loyal followings. Golf is highly resale-friendly because the buyer base is willing to pay used vs. new, and there's a strong Made-in-USA / Japan-built quality differentiation.",
  "field_workflow": [
    "Always identify the head + shaft separately — premium head + replaced cheap shaft = lower value",
    "Verify model name on the sole of the club (etched / printed)",
    "Year/generation matters: a 2024 Stealth 2 driver beats a 2018 M3 driver by 2-3x",
    "Stock vs upgraded shaft (e.g., Mitsubishi Diamana, Fujikura Ventus) — upgraded = premium",
    "Loft / lie / length adjustments — most modern drivers are adjustable, but irons aren't",
    "Right-hand vs left-hand: LH commands 10-20% premium because supply is smaller",
    "Women's vs men's: ladies-flex / shorter clubs comp separately",
    "Headcover + tool included = +5-10%"
  ],
